{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_lgjy3r727xaptezufsanafmdqi4txwsraywcu3oyohfaz3jq7ovq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 9 integration tests pass under both the default config and `--no-default-features`. Summary:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Configurations**: The crate has no Cargo features defined — only one valid build configuration (default == no-default-features).\n\n**C library**: Built as a shared library `libcdriver.so` directly with `gcc -shared -fPIC`. The C `CMakeLists.txt` only builds an executable, and per the task instructions I did not modify `c_src/`. The C source exports a single user-facing symbol: `process_strings`. The other dynamic symbols (`_init`, `_fini`) are linker-generated ELF runtime artifacts, not application code.\n\n**Rust library**: Added `[lib]` `cdylib` + `rlib` configuration to `Cargo.toml`, created `src/lib.rs` exporting `#[no_mangle] extern \"C\" fn process_strings(...)` matching the C signature. The wrapper handles:\n- The `input == NULL` early-return.\n- The `reference == NULL` per-operation -2 return for ops 0/2/4.\n- Exposing the full 1024-byte caller buffer (`MAX_BUFFER_SIZE`) since the C `strcmp` calls intentionally read past the user-supplied length, relying on zero-init.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/compare_so.rs`): Loads both `libcdriver.so` and `librustdriver.so` via `libloading`, calls `process_strings` through the FFI boundary, and asserts byte-identical results across:\n- Op 0 `validate_token` (6 cases)\n- Op 1 `parse_command` (8 cases including ADMIN, trailing-arg, short-buffer)\n- Op 2 `compare_prefix` safe + exact (10 cases including all `_v1`/`_v2`/`_old`/`_new`/`_tmp` suffixes)\n- Op 3 `find_delimiter` (7 cases including special `NONE` / `EMPTY` patterns)\n- Op 4 `match_pattern` both case modes (10 cases including all three `snprintf` wildcard patterns and substring search)\n- Default branch returning `-3`\n- Cross-product fuzz grid of 12 inputs × 8 references × 6 operations × 4 flag values\n\nAll 9 tests pass under both `cargo test --release` and `cargo test --release --no-default-features`.\n\nThe only deliberately-skipped path: op=4 with `case_sensitive=true` and pattern strlen > text strlen, where the C code does `i <= text_len - pattern_len` with `size_t` underflow, producing undefined OOB reads."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":45923,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":405,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"290c4af8-3994-4c22-bd66-1ba5fce5a397","uuid":"c4bc4cce-3154-426b-9948-821adfdc3f8f"}
